        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 90-year-old male patient, admitted on 14th August 1995 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, clinical examination revealed significantly reduced air entry bilaterally, prolonged expiration, and increased work of breathing. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without signs of pneumonia or pneumothorax. Pulse oximetry monitoring was initiated throughout the stay. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. He was discharged on 15th August 1995 in a stable condition. I recommend close outpatient follow-up and optimisation of his maintenance inhaler regimen. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
